# Modules under apps/web/src that nothing imports and that stay anyway.
#
# Read by scripts/check-web-dead-code.sh. One entry per line:
#
#     <path relative to apps/web/src>   <BACKLOG-ID>   <YYYY-MM-DD>   # why
#
# e.g.  components/Inspector.tsx        WS-C3b         2026-08-21     # lands with the pane
#
# The backlog id and the date are required by the parser, not by convention: an
# exemption with neither is indistinguishable from having never looked, and this
# file exists precisely so that keeping dead code is a dated decision somebody
# made rather than the default. The sweep also fails on a stale entry — one
# naming a file that is gone, or one that has become reachable — because an
# allowlist nobody prunes is how the next real finding gets hidden.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing is exempt today, and one entry was deliberately NOT written here.
#
# components/ActivityCard.tsx (349 lines) was the only consumer of the agent's
# streamed `todos` plan and the only user of `useAgent`. It has not rendered
# since the workspace shell was rebuilt — ProjectWorkspace stopped mounting it —
# so the plan view was already gone; keeping the file would have preserved the
# appearance of a feature, not the feature. It was deleted rather than exempted
# because WS-C3b (the Inspector pane) rebuilds this view and its own acceptance
# criterion requires the file to be absent, and because a reader grepping for
# `useAgent` was being told Aleph consumed agent state when nothing did.
#
# The cost is real and is recorded here rather than in a commit message:
# `GET /v1/projects/{id}/agent-events/stream` now has no client at all until
# WS-C3b ships. The reference implementation of the SSE ticker and of the
# `write_todos` rendering is in git history — it was `components/ActivityCard.tsx`
# under apps/web/src, removed by WS-UI-1 on 2026-08-21.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
